// The type rule of a binary operator: both operands have one type, and the
// operator is allowed on it (conf.id's bkk_allow lists the sub-operations by
// type: ints take everything, floats everything but %, strings + == and !=,
// lists nothing). A comparison or logical operator answers an int, any
// other the operand type. A mismatch is E0604, said once: an operand that
// was already wrong (-1) says nothing more.

